;;; outer-measure-construction.scm -- METHOD I OUTER MEASURES; the outer measure
;;; of a measure, its Caratheodory measure, completeness and the completion;
;;; Lebesgue outer measure on the line as an instance.
;;; Agent MEASURE-2, 2026-10-08 (scratchpad/triage/MEASURE-2.md).  Library:
;;; measure.  Helper prefix omc-.  43 theorems, every one `modulo 0' (oracles
;;; ineq, arith, crs).  Vocabulary: structure-library/outer-measure-construction.scm.
;;;
;;; THE NOTES' RESULTS (Thayer, Construction of Measures, Ch. 4 Sec. 2.1-2.2):
;;;   method-i-outer-is-outer-measure        Prop. 4.7 (Def. 4.8)
;;;   method-i-outer-of-measure              Remark 4.9, Eq. (81)
;;;   method-i-outer-extends                 Prop. 4.10: mu* extends rho
;;;   method-i-outer-measurable              Prop. 4.10: members of cA are mu*-measurable
;;;   method-i-outer-null-iff                Prop. 4.10: mu*-null = rho-null (Def. 3.1)
;;;   method-i-outer-finite-approx           Prop. 4.10: last assertion
;;;   method-i-outer-caratheodory-complete   Cor. 4.11, first half
;;;   method-i-outer-extends-completion      Cor. 4.11, second half (A u N measurable, value rho(A))
;;;   method-i-outer-sigma-finite-completion Prop. 4.12 (every measurable set is A u N)
;;;   lebesgue-premeasure, lebesgue-outer-measure, lebesgue-measure-complete,
;;;   interval-length-ccint                  the instance on the line
;;; AND THE BRICKS: cover-sums-{unfold,subset,elim,intro}, method-i-outer-{value,
;;; type,empty,mono,subadditive,le-single,attained,sigma-finite-approx},
;;; measure-is-premeasure, cover-sum-dominates, caratheodory-measure-complete (for
;;; ANY outer measure), sigma-algebra-countable-inter; and the [0,+inf] sums the
;;; eps / 2^(i+1) argument needs: einf-lt-witness, rps-le-of-forall-eps, eplus-swap4,
;;; rps-prefix-add, esum-nn-add-le, esum-nn-term-le, esum-nn-zero,
;;; dyadic-eps-{type,prefix,sum-le} (eps * 2^-(i+1), through dyadic-weights.scm),
;;; trinum-ge, nn-unpair-le, rps-finsum-fiber-le and esum-nn-flatten-le (THE DOUBLE
;;; SUM: re-indexing a doubly indexed family by the Cantor code does not increase
;;; its sum -- two fiber decompositions, finsum-cm-fiber-ptwise).
;;;
;;; WHERE THE PROOFS LEAVE THE NOTES (each a finding of the report):
;;;   * Prop. 4.7: the countable choice of the covers is a CHOICE over the set of good
;;;     covers, skolemised (dk-abstract!); the double series sum_i sum_j is bounded by
;;;     esum-nn-flatten-le; the case mu*(E_i) = +inf is split off first.
;;;   * Prop. 4.10: "without loss of generality non-increasing" and Prop. 1.18 are not
;;;     needed -- rho(n_n A_n) <= rho(A_n) <= mu*(E) + 1/(n+1) by monotonicity alone
;;;     (method-i-outer-attained); the step "by the argument used in the preceding
;;;     paragraph" is that lemma.
;;;   * Prop. 4.12: the notes show only E inside F in cA with F \ E null; the A u N
